n-forces-pti-retreat-imrans-party-likely-to-postpone-sept-27-islamabad-march-to-oct-4/articleshow/134487316.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/pakistan/pakistan-govt-crackdown-forces-pti-retreat-imrans-party-likely-to-postpone-sept-27-islamabad-march-to-oct-4/articleshow/134487316.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-25T20:01:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Karan Manral</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134487780,imgsize-697370.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Cambridge narrows probe into late professor Jason Arday’s hiring, drops plagiarism focus]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134487692.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/cambridge-narrows-probe-into-late-professor-jason-ardays-hiring-drops-plagiarism-focus/articleshow/134487692.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/cambridge-narrows-probe-into-late-professor-jason-ardays-hiring-drops-plagiarism-focus/articleshow/134487692.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-25T19:57:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Gokul Ankari</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134487776,imgsize-667350.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[China's coal mines may offer a new water source for data centre cooling]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134485430.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/chinas-coal-mines-generate-billions-of-cubic-metres-of-water-researchers-say-it-could-help-cool-data-centres/articleshow/134485430.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/chinas-coal-mines-generate-billions-of-cubic-metres-of-water-researchers-say-it-could-help-cool-data-centres/articleshow/134485430.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-25T19:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134485635,imgsize-149232.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A Michigan family lost a home of $194,400 over a $2,242 tax bill; the county sold it for $76,008]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134487034.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The United States Supreme Court has made a landmark decision stating that tax sale compensation must be based on the auction price rather than the assessed value of a property. A family in Michigan, burdened with a $2,241.93 tax debt, faced foreclosure despite their home being valued at $194,400. With the auction yielding only $76,008, the family is rightfully awarded the remaining $73,766.07, reinforcing constitutional guidelines for future tax sales.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-michigan-family-lost-a-home-assessed-at-194400-over-a-disputed-2242-property-tax-bill-the-county-sold-it-for-76008-the-buyer-resold-it-for-195000-and-the-supreme-court-vacated-the-lower-ruling-in-2026/articleshow/134487034.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-michigan-family-lost-a-home-assessed-at-194400-over-a-disputed-2242-property-tax-bill-the-county-sold-it-for-76008-the-buyer-resold-it-for-195000-and-the-supreme-court-vacated-the-lower-ruling-in-2026/articleshow/134487034.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-25T19:46:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134487609,imgsize-1882044.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Sikh woman in Canada killed at home; neighbors saw her mother frantically running out with grandkids]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134487548.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/sikh-woman-in-canada-killed-at-home-neighbors-saw-her-mother-frantically-running-out-with-grandkids/articleshow/134487548.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/sikh-woman-in-canada-killed-at-home-neighbors-saw-her-mother-frantically-running-out-with-grandkids/articleshow/134487548.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-25T19:44:36+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134487597,imgsize-35374.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A US couple lost a mortgage-free home of $59,759 after a $588.21 tax debt grew to $5,268]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134486717.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Nebraska couple, Kevin Fair and Terry Fair, lost their home due to unpaid property taxes totaling $588. After being unable to pay the amount required to redeem their property, Continental Resources obtained a tax deed. Fair claimed that losing property worth $59,759 for such a small tax debt constituted an unconstitutional taking. The Nebraska Supreme Court ruled Fair had a valid takings claim based on property value.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-nebraska-couple-lost-a-mortgage-free-home-assessed-at-59759-after-a-588-21-tax-debt-grew-to-5268-32-the-us-supreme-court-sent-the-case-back-and-nebraskas-top-court-revived-the-compensation-claim/articleshow/134486717.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-nebraska-couple-lost-a-mortgage-free-home-assessed-at-59759-after-a-588-21-tax-debt-grew-to-5268-32-the-us-supreme-court-sent-the-case-back-and-nebraskas-top-court-revived-the-compensation-claim/articleshow/134486717.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-25T19:07:43+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134486917,imgsize-1028691.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Trump gives 'totally unacceptable' warning to Xi over China helping Iran]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134486490.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Donald Trump told Xi Jinping that any assistance China provides to Iran is unacceptable during his visit. The two leaders held a closed-door meeting to discuss various critical global issues, including trade and military matters. Trump organized a state dinner attended by key US technology executives to enhance relations. The visit coincided with China's Mid-Autumn Festival, marking a time for family gatherings and festivities.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/totally-unacceptable-trump-xi-talked-about-china-helping-iran-says-us-envoy/articleshow/134486490.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/totally-unacceptable-trump-xi-talked-about-china-helping-iran-says-us-envoy/articleshow/134486490.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-25T18:59:46+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134486780,imgsize-102882.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Kentucky woman turned 45 acres into a nature preserve; sewer project now takes seven easements]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134483477.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Kentucky woman spent 35 years turning her 45-acre property into a natural area she planned to preserve through the Boone Conservancy. A nearly $40 million sewer project secured seven easements across her land through eminent domain. After a court backed SD1’s acquisition, neighbours protested and Boone County officials asked the utility to explain why it chose the route.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-kentucky-woman-spent-35-years-turning-45-acres-into-a-nature-preserve-now-a-nearly-40-million-sewer-project-has-secured-seven-easements-across-her-land-through-eminent-domain-triggering-fresh-county-scrutiny/articleshow/134483477.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-kentucky-woman-spent-35-years-turning-45-acres-into-a-nature-preserve-now-a-nearly-40-million-sewer-project-has-secured-seven-easements-across-her-land-through-eminent-domain-triggering-fresh-county-scrutiny/articleshow/134483477.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-25T19:01:52+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134484181,imgsize-193542.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A Texas oil geologist first saw McKittrick Canyon in 1921, later bought the land for a private retreat]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134484619.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Wallace Pratt's journey began in 1921 when he stumbled upon the breathtaking McKittrick Canyon, igniting a passionate fascination with its natural features. He bought land in the area and raised two residences, one of which was Ship on the Desert. Following the passing of his first spouse, Pratt continued his conservation journey alongside Iris Calderhead, eventually donating 5,600 acres to the federal government.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-texas-oil-geologist-first-saw-mckittrick-canyon-in-1921-later-bought-the-land-for-a-private-retreat-38-years-later-he-donated-4942-acres-and-his-home-helping-create-guadalupe-mountains-national-park/articleshow/134484619.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-texas-oil-geologist-first-saw-mckittrick-canyon-in-1921-later-bought-the-land-for-a-private-retreat-38-years-later-he-donated-4942-acres-and-his-home-helping-create-guadalupe-mountains-national-park/articleshow/134484619.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-25T18:52:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134486622,imgsize-1802715.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[1892 painting seized from Munich widow returned to US heirs after Nazi persecution]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134485091.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-painting-seized-from-a-munich-bankers-widow-during-nazi-persecution-has-been-returned-to-her-us-heirs-after-decades-of-uncertainty-provenance-researchers-traced-the-1892-work-through-wartime-records-and-museum-archives/articleshow/134485091.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-painting-seized-from-a-munich-bankers-widow-during-nazi-persecution-has-been-returned-to-her-us-heirs-after-decades-of-uncertainty-provenance-researchers-traced-the-1892-work-through-wartime-records-and-museum-archives/articleshow/134485091.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-25T18:12:35+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134485146,imgsize-540918.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Tamil H-1B man with disability reaches out to Indian-origin Democrat leader after being fired; Suhas Subramanyam shuts trolls, says 'Yes I help everyone']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134485247.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/tamil-h-1b-man-with-disability-reaches-out-to-indian-origin-democrat-leader-after-being-fired-suhas-subramanyam-shuts-trolls-says-yes-i-help-everyone/articleshow/134485247.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/tamil-h-1b-man-with-disability-reaches-out-to-indian-origin-democrat-leader-after-being-fired-suhas-subramanyam-shuts-trolls-says-yes-i-help-everyone/articleshow/134485247.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-25T17:54:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134485578,imgsize-66228.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[NASA sent 12.5M tomato seeds to space in 1984; by 1990, 40,000 schools in 40 countries grew them]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134482170.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In 1984, NASA initiated the SEEDS project aimed at exploring how the space environment affects plant growth. Participants, comprising approximately 3.3 million students from diverse educational backgrounds worldwide, received kits that included seeds launched into space and Earth-based controls for comparison. Preliminary findings indicated a marginally enhanced germination rate for the seeds sent to space, though notable growth differences diminished during the plants' life cycles.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/space/in-1984-nasa-sent-12-5-million-tomato-seeds-to-space-in-1990-they-had-to-be-brought-back-to-earth-and-were-planted-across-40000-schools-in-30-countries/articleshow/134482170.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/space/in-1984-nasa-sent-12-5-million-tomato-seeds-to-space-in-1990-they-had-to-be-brought-back-to-earth-and-were-planted-across-40000-schools-in-30-countries/articleshow/134482170.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-25T17:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134486104,imgsize-193878.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Retired UK rail engineer turns East Sussex garden into 50-foot railway with solar-powered trolley]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134482007.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Adrian Backshall transformed his East Sussex garden into a working railway, inspired by his railway engineering career. The garden features a unique 50-foot railway with a solar-powered system and authentic railway memorabilia. Initially a lockdown project, it has evolved to include a Victorian-style carriage for entertaining guests. Backshall's project reflects a blend of history and engineering, following his retirement from Network Rail.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-retired-uk-rail-engineer-turned-his-east-sussex-garden-into-a-working-railway-using-a-victorian-platelayers-trolley-the-line-now-runs-50-feet-and-uses-a-12-volt-battery-charged-by-solar-power/articleshow/134482007.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-retired-uk-rail-engineer-turned-his-east-sussex-garden-into-a-workin